### Converse API > toolConfig

Source: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/conversation-inference.md

The `toolConfig` field allows you to define a tool for the model to use in generating a response.

--------------------------------

### API Reference/Amazon Bedrock Runtime/Converse API/Request Body

Source: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_runtime_Converse.md

The Request Body for the Converse API is an array of SystemContentBlock objects. It is not required. The toolConfig parameter is also not required and is of type ToolConfiguration object. It provides configuration information for the tools that the model can use when generating a response. For information about models that support tool use, see Supported models and model features.

